{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:693c559e842aadf93ddcaba5f140c97aac1419c23fda3c1038c7a690c13b1213", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Section 1\nThe Guardian newspaper has issued a corrections statement addressing several inaccuracies found in its recent publications. The corrections span multiple articles published on August 25th, covering a range of topics from crime to history and current events. The paper emphasizes its commitment to accuracy and transparency in its reporting. Several instances involved misrepresenting individuals' roles or affiliations, as well as factual errors regarding events and backgrounds. The corrections are intended to rectify these errors and provide readers with the correct information.\n\n***\n\nSection 2\nOne correction clarifies the geographical scope of a new pet theft law, stating it applies specifically to England and Northern Ireland, not the entire UK as previously reported. Another correction addresses a misattribution of the title \"founder\" to Eileen Burbidge of Fertifa, clarifying that she is the executive director while Tony Chen and Nick Kuan are the company's founders. Additionally, a correction was made regarding a quote from Juliet Stevenson in a Q&A interview, clarifying that she referred to her work with director Alex Lawther, not \"Lowther.\"\n\nSection 3\n* The article regarding the pet theft law incorrectly stated its UK-wide application; it is limited to England and Northern Ireland.\n* Eileen Burbidge was mistakenly referred to as the \"founder\" of Fertifa; she is the executive director, with Tony Chen and Nick Kuan being the founders.\n\nSection 4\nThe corrections also include a clarification about the ethnicity of the family featured in the film *Bend It Like Beckham* (they are Sikh, not Muslim), and a correction concerning the religious conversion of Venetia Stanley's father (it was her uncle, the third Baron Stanley, who converted to Islam). Furthermore, the statement that Pavel Durov, the founder of the Telegram app, was arrested at a French airport is also mentioned. The paper encourages readers to direct any further corrections to the Readers’ Editor via email or telephone.\n\nP.P.S. The Guardian's commitment to accurate reporting is evident in its prompt issuance of these corrections, demonstrating a dedication to maintaining journalistic integrity.\n\n\n\nWrite to the Readers’ Editor, the Observer, York Way, London N1 9GU, email observer.readers@observer.co.uk, tel 020 3353 4736", "logprobs": [{"token": "Section", "logprob": -0.00035482310340739787}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.3870933949947357}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -0.04426185041666031}, {"token": "▁Guardian", "logprob": -0.004114971030503511}, {"token": "▁newspaper", "logprob": -0.4997393488883972}, {"token": "▁has", "logprob": -0.03216397762298584}, {"token": "▁issued", "logprob": -0.02976951003074646}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.9185600280761719}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.2913370728492737}, {"token": "▁statement", "logprob": -0.12868136167526245}, {"token": "▁addressing", "logprob": -0.5043028593063354}, {"token": "▁several", "logprob": -0.023615637794137}, {"token": "▁inaccuracies", "logprob": -1.0549803972244263}, {"token": "▁found", "logprob": -0.03601362183690071}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.0120955565944314}, {"token": "▁its", "logprob": -0.03561796993017197}, {"token": "▁recent", "logprob": -0.18943902850151062}, {"token": "▁publications", "logprob": -0.06740330904722214}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.025500327348709106}, {"token": "▁The", "logprob": -0.2799065411090851}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.7393750548362732}, {"token": "▁span", "logprob": -1.7405728101730347}, {"token": "▁multiple", "logprob": -1.6798627376556396}, {"token": "▁articles", "logprob": -2.1219027985353023e-05}, {"token": "▁published", "logprob": -0.007694960571825